sequenceDiagram
    actor C as Customer
    participant G as gshop
    participant K as cart-service
    participant O as order-service
    participant I as inventory-service
    participant P as payment-service
    participant F as fulfilment-service
    participant N as notification-service

    Note over G,N: Scenario A — reservation fails (bulk, all-or-nothing)
    G->>O: POST /orders {items, shippingAddress, paymentMethodId}
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations {orderId, items[A, B, C]}
    I-->>O: 409 {failures: [B insufficient_stock, C unknown_sku]}
    Note over O,I: Nothing was reserved — no release needed
    O-->>G: 409 {error, reservationFailures [B, C]}
    Note over O,N: No order row, no order event, no email
    G->>G: show every failed line + Remove action
    C->>G: Remove B and C
    G->>K: DELETE /carts/{id}/items/{sku} (per removed line)
    K-->>G: 200 {items}
    G->>O: retry POST /orders (remaining items)

    Note over G,N: Scenario B — authorization declined (synchronous)
    O->>P: POST /payments/authorize {orderId, amountCents, paymentMethodId}
    P-->>O: 402 {error, reason}
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations/{orderId}/release<br/>(idempotent compensation)
    O-->>G: 402 {error, paymentFailure {reason}}
    Note over O,N: No order row, no email — customer fixes card<br/>and retries in-session (cart unchanged).

    Note over G,N: Scenario B2 — unknown paymentMethodId
    O->>P: POST /payments/authorize {..., paymentMethodId}
    P-->>O: 404 {error: "Payment method not found"}
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations/{orderId}/release<br/>(idempotent compensation)
    O-->>G: 400 {error: "Payment method not found"}

    Note over G,N: Scenario B3 — payment-service unavailable (breaker open)
    G->>O: POST /orders {items, shippingAddress, paymentMethodId}
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations {orderId, items[]}
    I-->>O: 201 {orderId, items}
    O-xP: POST /payments/authorize (breaker OPEN)
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations/{orderId}/release<br/>(idempotent compensation)
    O-->>G: 503 {error: "Payment service unavailable"}
    Note over O,I: Fail-fast before reserving is deferred (TD-9):<br/>the reserve happens first and is released here.

    Note over G,N: Scenario B3b — authorize call fails mid-request (timeout / 5xx)
    O-xP: POST /payments/authorize
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations/{orderId}/release<br/>(idempotent compensation)
    O-->>G: 503 {error: "Payment service unavailable"}
    Note over O,P: If the authorize landed behind the timeout, the orphan hold<br/>is only recovered by the expiry sweep — US-20, not yet built.

    Note over G,N: Scenario B4 — persisting the order fails after a 200 authorize
    O->>O: persist order (transaction fails)
    O->>I: POST /inventorys/order-reservations/{orderId}/release<br/>(idempotent compensation)
    O->>P: void authorization — no void endpoint yet —<br/>hold recovery is the US-20 sweep (not yet built)
    O-->>G: 500 {error}

    Note over G,N: Scenario C — authorization expires before dispatch
    alt US-20 — not yet built (no producer)
        P->>P: sweep {status: authorized, expiresAt < now}
        P-->>O: payment-events: PaymentAuthorizationExpired {orderId}
        P-->>I: payment-events: PaymentAuthorizationExpired {orderId}
        P-->>F: payment-events: PaymentAuthorizationExpired {orderId}
        O->>O: status = cancelled (consumer built)
        O--)N: order-events: OrderCancelled {orderId}
        I->>I: release reservations (US-20.3 — not built)
        F->>F: cancel in-flight pick/pack (US-20.4 — not built)
        N->>N: enqueue "Your order was cancelled" email
    end
    Note over P,N: US-20 — not yet built: payment-service has no sweep/producer —<br/>order-service consumes PaymentAuthorizationExpired (built), notification receives OrderCancelled,<br/>inventory/fulfilment consumers do not exist.

    Note over G,N: Scenario D — dispatch fails (warehouse exception)
    F--)O: fulfilment-events: DispatchFailed {orderId, reason}
    F--)P: fulfilment-events: DispatchFailed
    F--)N: fulfilment-events: DispatchFailed
    O->>O: status = dispatch_failed
    O->>I: release reservations (idempotent)
    P->>P: void authorization (publishes nothing)
    N->>N: enqueue "We couldn't ship your order" email
    Note over O,N: Notification consumes fulfilment-events directly —<br/>order-service does not publish a dispatch-failed order event.

    Note over G,N: Scenario E — capture fails after dispatch
    P->>P: capture fails (DispatchConfirmed consumed)
    P--)O: payment-events: PaymentFailed {orderId, reason: capture_failed}
    P--)N: payment-events: PaymentFailed {orderId, reason: capture_failed}
    O->>O: status = payment_failed<br/>+ order_reconciliation row
    O--)N: order-events: OrderPaymentFailed {orderId, reason: capture_failed}
    N->>N: enqueue "We couldn't take your payment" email<br/>and "We couldn't process your payment" email
    Note over O,I: Items may already be shipped —<br/>manual reconciliation, no automatic release.

    Note over G,N: Scenario F — customer cancels an authorized order
    G->>O: PATCH /orders/{id} {"status": "cancelled"}
    O->>O: status = cancelled (authorized only)
    O--)N: order-events: OrderCancelled {orderId}
    N->>N: enqueue "Your order was cancelled" email
    Note over O,I: Inventory reservations are NOT released — known gap.
